@startuml tor-request-flow

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #3498DB
    ActorBorderColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #BDC3C7
}

title User Request Flow through Onion Routing System

actor Browser
participant "Tor Client" as Client #2ECC71
participant "Discovery\nService (gRPC)" as Discovery #F39C12
participant "Entry Relay" as Entry #8E44AD
participant "Middle Relay" as Middle #9B59B6
participant "Exit Relay" as Exit #A569BD
participant "Website" as Web #1ABC9C

== Relay Registration ==

Entry -> Discovery: RegisterNode RPC
activate Discovery
Discovery --> Entry: Registered
deactivate Discovery

Middle -> Discovery: RegisterNode RPC
activate Discovery
Discovery --> Middle: Registered
deactivate Discovery

Exit -> Discovery: RegisterNode RPC
activate Discovery
Discovery --> Exit: Registered
deactivate Discovery

== Node Discovery ==

Browser -> Client: SOCKS5 CONNECT\nexample.com:443
activate Browser
activate Client

Client -> Discovery: GetRandomPath(count=3) RPC
activate Discovery
Discovery --> Client: [Entry, Middle, Exit]\nnode descriptors
deactivate Discovery

Client -> Client: Build circuit:\nCREATE -> Entry\nEXTEND -> Middle\nEXTEND -> Exit

== Request Phase ==

Client -> Client: onion_encrypt(data, 3 layers)
note right of Client
  Layer 1 (outer): Entry key
  Layer 2 (middle): Middle key
  Layer 3 (inner): Exit key
end note

Client -> Entry: TCP Send cell\n[E1(E2(E3(data)))]
activate Entry

Entry -> Entry: Decrypt outer layer\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
note right: Result: [E2(E3(data))]

Entry -> Middle: TCP Forward cell\n[E2(E3(data))]
activate Middle

Middle -> Middle: Decrypt middle layer\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
note right: Result: [E3(data)]

Middle -> Exit: TCP Forward cell\n[E3(data)]
activate Exit

Exit -> Exit: Decrypt inner layer\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
note right: Result: Plaintext

Exit -> Web: TCP Connect + HTTP Request
activate Web

Web --> Exit: HTTP Response\n200 OK + HTML
deactivate Web

== Response Phase ==

Exit -> Exit: Encrypt with exit key\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
Exit -> Middle: TCP Send cell\n[E3(response)]
deactivate Exit

Middle -> Middle: Encrypt with middle key\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
Middle -> Entry: TCP Send cell\n[E2(E3(response))]
deactivate Middle

Entry -> Entry: Encrypt with entry key\n(stateful AES-128-CTR)
Entry -> Client: TCP Send cell\n[E1(E2(E3(response)))]
deactivate Entry

Client -> Client: onion_decrypt(data, 3 layers)
note right of Client
  Reverse order:
  Layer 1 (entry) -> Layer 2 (middle) -> Layer 3 (exit)
end note

Client --> Browser: SOCKS5 Response\nHTML content
deactivate Client

Browser -> Browser: Render page
deactivate Browser

@enduml
